   This permits linking libblks_core.a, include/blks.h, and using the Rust crate
   from projects under any license (including MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD, or commercial),
   while ensuring that any modifications, improvements, or bugfixes to the blks-core
   engine itself must remain open source under LGPL-3.0-or-later.

2. `blks-cli` (Command-Line Interface Binary):
   Licensed under the GNU General Public License v3 or later (GPL-3.0-or-later).
   See LICENSE.GPL for full terms.
   The terminal application is strictly protected under strong copyleft.
